  "answer_text": "What a classic! Here's everything you need to know about that iconic scene:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udf7a Del Falls Through the Bar \u2014 *\"Yuppy Love\"*\n\n**\"Yuppy Love\"** was the first episode of Series 6 of *Only Fools and Horses*, airing on **8th January 1989** on BBC1, with a viewing figure of **13.9 million**.\n\nDel Boy's fall through the bar has become one of the **most celebrated sitcom scenes ever**. The scene was recently voted the **number one comedy moment of all time** in a UK poll.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcfa What Happens in the Scene\n\nThe barman lifts up the bar flap. Del is unaware of this, tells Trigger they may be in with their luck and to \"play it nice and cool.\" As he goes to lean on the bar, he falls right over. Trigger looks around wondering where Del has gone. Del gets up and tells Trig they're leaving.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfac Behind the Scenes\n\n- The scene was inspired by writer **John Sullivan** watching a man do the exact same thing in a real wine bar \u2014 except the man grabbed onto the fixed part of the bar so he didn't fall all the way over. Sullivan thought it funny for the man's body language, trying to recover his cool.\n\n- Sullivan wanted a slip, stumble, and a tree-like fall; **David Jason** thought Del should go all the way over \u2014 starting to go sideways, then going over **without looking** in the direction of the fall, which Jason thought was the key to the scene.\n\n- There was a hidden crash mat, but it was a hard shot to get because it was difficult not to look where Jason was falling \u2014 Jason had done a number of falls in the theatre, so that came in handy.\n\n- A rehearsal script for the episode that went up for auction showed that **Trigger wasn't supposed to be in the scene originally**. However, the story goes that Roger Lloyd Pack was there on the day and John Sullivan decided he should be there after all.\n\n- They got Trigger's blue suit and stuck him in the scene, which was **mostly improvised**.\n\n- Just as funny as Del's fall was **Trigger's baffled reaction** to Del's sudden disappearance.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83c\udfc6 Legacy\n\nThe scene where Del Boy falls through the bar was voted the **best scene in the entire sitcom** by fans in a poll by RadioTimes.com. David Jason gets people asking him about that fall all the time, and some never like to talk about anything else, but he's happy to be remembered for something so iconic.\n\nDel falling through the bar was even the inspiration behind a scene 25 years later in a mini episode for **Sport Relief in March 2014**, where Del and Rodney meet **David Beckham** \u2014 and Beckham himself falls to the floor after leaning on a portable rack that has been moved.",
